The objective is to maximize the sum of a sequence of numbers by changing the sign of exactly k numbers. The sequence is sorted in non-decreasing order.

The optimal strategy is to first change the signs of the negative numbers. If k is greater than or equal to the number of negative numbers, then change the sign of all negative numbers.  If k is still greater than zero, then we have two cases.
1. The smallest absolute value is zero. In this case, we don't change the sign of zero.
2. The smallest absolute value is non-zero. In this case, if k is even, we don't need to make any changes to the positive numbers. If k is odd, we change the sign of the smallest number twice, resulting in a net change of multiplying the smallest number by -1.

