We need to find the shortest and lexicographically smallest string that is not a substring of any of the given strings. We can iterate through possible lengths starting from 1. For each length, we can generate all possible strings of lowercase English letters of that length, and check if any of the given strings contain them as substrings. If a string is not a substring of any of the given strings, we return it. If we reach a length where all strings of that length are substrings of at least one of the given strings, we increment the length and repeat the process.

