The core idea is to repeatedly apply the division operation whenever possible. If at any point, applying division leads to a state where we're stuck and can't reach all 1s, then we need to increment adjacent numbers. A BFS or DFS type search might be generally needed, even though the problem statement provides enough context to suggest that repeatedly applying division and then incrementing may work. However, there is an upper bound on the operations (1000).
