The code implements a constructive algorithm to generate the adjacency matrix for a graph with *n* nodes, where all cycle tours have the same total price. The algorithm works by constructing a special sequence `b` and using it to calculate the edge weights.

The `constructRow(n)` function computes the special sequence `b` of length `n + 1`. The idea is to generate distinct numbers `b[i]` such that `b[k]` is distinct for all k, and also ensure no duplicate edge values arise later.

The `constructMatrix(b, n)` function uses sequence `b` to generate a matrix such that the cost of all cycles is same. Specifically, it assigns `b[i]` to the edges connecting node 1 to node *i*. Inner edges are assigned `b[i]+b[j]+x-b[2]-b[3]` (*x* is selected so that the total price is distinct with all chosen prices).

The `main` part reads `n`, constructs `b`, constructs `a` and then prints the desired matrix. The code already works, the code can be organized to improve readability for variables, and reduce the line length.

