### Reasoning

If n * m == 2, then it is impossible to visit all cells and return to (1,1) without visiting a cell twice, besides (1,1). Because we need to visit n*m cells plus the starting cell (1,1). Thus there are n*m + 1 steps. The only step available other than to the start, is from (1,1) to the only neighbor, (1,2) or (2,1), and returning will mean we visit it twice. With just two cells it requires us to visit the other once and return home, totaling three visits, and requiring two visits to the other cells, one extra.
If either n or m == 1, say n==1, then we zig zag between available columns.
If n is odd, or m is odd, we can traverse the whole board in a snake like manner.
If both n and m are even, then we will need a teleporter. We traverse almost all except for one cell to the right of the bottom right (i.e. (n, m-1) ). Then (n,m-1) will need a teleporter to (1,1).
Also if n == m == 2, we require no teleporters.

### Code

