The problem asks us to count right triangles formed by '*' characters on an n x m grid, with the legs of the right angle parallel to the axes. This means that for any right triangle, two of its vertices must share either the same row or the same column.

We can iterate through each cell in the grid. If a cell contains an asterisk, we can consider it as the vertex of the right angle. Then, we need to count how many other asterisks are in the same row and how many other asterisks are in the same column. The product of these two counts will give the number of right triangles that can be formed with the current asterisk as the right angle vertex. We sum up these counts for all asterisk cells to get the final result.

