The problem requires us to count the number of admissible temperatures within a given range [a, b]. A temperature is admissible if at least k recipes recommend it. We are given n recipes, each specifying a range [l, r] of recommended temperatures.

The core idea is to use a difference array (or prefix sum) to efficiently track the number of recipes recommending each temperature. We create an array `counts` of size 200001 (since the maximum temperature is 200000). For each recipe [l, r], we increment `counts[l]` and decrement `counts[r+1]`. This way, when we calculate the prefix sum of `counts`, `counts[i]` will store the number of recipes recommending temperature `i`.

After calculating the prefix sum, we iterate through `counts` and create a new array `admissible` where `admissible[i]` is 1 if `counts[i]` >= k, and 0 otherwise. Finally, we compute the prefix sum of `admissible` to efficiently answer the queries. For each query [a, b], the number of admissible temperatures within this range is simply `admissible[b] - admissible[a-1]`.

